' bug-464: a connected `tls::Socket` moves to another thread and keeps talking.
'
' The handshake completes HERE, on the main thread; every byte of the exchange
' happens on the worker, over the SAME session. That is the property the widened
' transfer copy buys -- the socket's live session state (`SSL*`/`SSL_CTX*` on
' OpenSSL, the SSPI block on Schannel, the connection ctx / dispatch queue on
' macOS) has to arrive intact for the worker's `tls::write` to encrypt under the
' negotiated keys.
'
' Peer is 8.8.8.8:443 (Google Public DNS -- stable anycast, HTTPS, cert SANs the
' bare IP), validated against dns.google, matching the sibling `tls-poll-rt` and
' `tls-connect-google-rt` fixtures. Output is one Boolean so the golden does not
' depend on the remote's response bytes.
IMPORT io
IMPORT thread
IMPORT tls
IMPORT xfer_tls_worker

FUNC main AS Integer
  LET t AS Thread OF RES tls::Socket TO Boolean = thread::start(xfer_tls_worker::talkOnTransferredSocket, "dns.google")
  RES conn = tls::connect("8.8.8.8", 443, 30000, "dns.google")
  thread::transfer(t, conn)
  io::print("moved=" & toString(thread::waitFor(t)))
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
